{
  "id": "u12-l03",
  "unit": "u12-have-to",
  "title": "You don't have to",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**Add না for 'don't have to'.** **তোমাকে আসতে হবে না** means 'you don't have to come': there's no need. It does **not** mean 'you mustn't come'.\n\nA friendly one to know: **চিন্তা করতে হবে না** 'no need to worry'.\n\n**Ask with a question word** before the -তে form: **আমাকে কী করতে হবে?** 'What do I have to do?', **কখন যেতে হবে?** 'When do (we) have to go?' The person can be left out when it's clear.\n\n**দিতে** 'to give' also means 'to pay': **এখানে টাকা দিতে হবে না** 'You don't have to pay here'.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "dite",
      "bn": "দিতে",
      "tr": "dite",
      "en": "to give",
      "notes": "Infinitive of দেওয়া. টাকা দিতে হবে \"(you) have to pay\"."
    },
    {
      "id": "nite",
      "bn": "নিতে",
      "tr": "nite",
      "en": "to take",
      "notes": "Infinitive of নেওয়া."
    },
    {
      "id": "chinta",
      "bn": "চিন্তা",
      "tr": "chinta",
      "en": "worry",
      "notes": "চিন্তা করা \"to worry\". চিন্তা করতে হবে না \"no need to worry; don't worry\"."
    }
  ],
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "e01",
      "type": "select_translation",
      "prompt": {
        "bn": "তোমাকে আসতে হবে না।",
        "tr": "tomake ashte hobe na.",
        "en": "You don't have to come.",
        "alt": [
          "You needn't come."
        ]
      },
      "direction": "bn_to_en",
      "options": [
        "You have to come.",
        "You don't have to come.",
        "You can't come.",
        "You didn't come."
      ],
      "answer": 1,
      "why": "**-তে হবে না** = \"don't have to\" (no need). It does not mean \"mustn't\"."
    },
